- a#14 (005 percent-encoded Hangul body link), b#8 (011 Invest Taiwan lang=jpn): ACCEPTED-uk says skip; hard rule
  forbids changing links/hrefs. Both hrefs left byte-identical. Link LABELS read naturally, so no relabel needed.
- Frontmatter `url:` containing Hangul (008, 009): skipped per ACCEPTED-uk (canonical source metadata, not rendered).
- a#32 / b#14 THOUSANDS SEPARATOR — PARTIALLY SKIPPED (checker-forced). Ukrainian wants a space (1 579 589).
  scripts/check-column-translation.mjs `analyzeNumbers` accepts ONLY `.` or `,` as a group separator
  (coeff = \d{1,3}(?:[.,]\d{3})+ ...). Verified empirically: '500 000' (ASCII, U+00A0, U+202F, U+2009) all tokenise
  as [500, 0] -> "missing from translation" -> numbers FAIL. Per WO §Verify ("prefer the form the checker accepts
  and note it"), TWD 1.579.589 / TWD 500.000 / TWD 25.000.000 etc. keep the existing dot grouping.
  What WAS fixed in the same rows: decimal comma (0.5 -> 0,5 in 008; 0.5 -> 0,5 metre in 012), kg -> кг (010),
  and all slash/ISO dates -> Ukrainian words (the checker parses Ukrainian month names, verified).
  Also NOT changed: 'TWD 1.57M' in guidanceTeamBios.uk — GUIDANCE_BIO_PRESERVED_TERMS requires it byte-identical
  in all 27 locales (src/data/__tests__/guidance-team-bios.test.ts); changing uk alone breaks the cross-locale
  contract and the other 26 locales are out of this WO's write scope. Flagged for the supervisor.
- b#2 "3 особи спадкують по 1/3" (016 faq + §1): left as a digit — it is a real count of three heirs
  (ACCEPTED-uk says leave).
- 002 §5 "не може за 1 раз перевищувати 1 рік": the two digits are kept because the Korean source
  ("1회 휴업 기간은 1년을 넘을 수 없습니다") contributes two `1` tokens; dropping either FAILs `numbers`.
  The unreadable comma-parenthetical ("не може, 1 раз, перевищити") — the actual a#47 complaint — is gone.

