== DISAGREEMENTS WITH THE REVIEWERS (NOT applied) ==
1. a#32 / b#14 thousands separator "1 579 589 TWD": the reviewer is right about Ukrainian typography but the
   repo checker cannot parse space-grouped numbers (see SKIPPED above). Fixing this properly needs a change to
   scripts/check-column-translation.mjs (accept \s/U+00A0/U+202F as a group separator) — outside this WO's
   write scope. Supervisor decision needed.
2. a#32 "TWD 1.57M" in the team bio: cannot be localised without breaking GUIDANCE_BIO_PRESERVED_TERMS for all
   27 locales. Not applied; needs a cross-locale decision.
3. a#54 (005 Q1) and a#57 (007) as worded: both suggested telling the reader what applies "для читачів з України"
   / naming Ukraine in the cross-border family example. ACCEPTED-uk forbids statements about the reader's own
   country, and the `nationality` checker rule fails on a nationality present in the target but absent from the
   source. Applied the neutral R2 generalisation instead.
4. a#14 / b#8 (Hangul-slug body link in 005; Invest Taiwan lang=jpn in 011): the reviewer is factually right that
   a /uk/ reader is sent to a Korean-slug page and a Japanese-language page. ACCEPTED-uk marks these as already
   handled and the hard rules forbid touching links, so nothing was changed. Still open.
5. b#22 / a#59 ROC-year glosses: added "(2023)" / "(2020)" only on first mention in the body; adding the Gregorian
   year to every repetition would pile up "extra in translation" number warnings for no reader benefit.
6. 007: did NOT rename 戶政機關 / 戶籍法 / 戶政事務所 away from "орган цивільного стану" / "Закон про цивільний
   стан". In 007 these bodies really do register marriage and divorce, and "цивільний стан" is what a Ukrainian
   family lawyer writes; the literal "реєстрація домогосподарств" would read worse. R8's 戶籍 gloss was applied
   where 戶籍 stands alone (007 intro, 016, 017 — where it is a business/estate registration, i.e. b#10's case).

